v26.03.03 - OSS preparation - md files created, device serves info page.
v26.03.02 - Build improvements.
            Debug macros renamed.
v26.03.01 - Use MCPWM capture block for PWM.
            Flashing script allows upload only option.
v26.02.08 - Early boot log support (with optional email).
            Fast boot failure - board halt if fails arise before config
            processing put the device into AP mode. 
            Flat config.dat replaced with json, and sensor/lg configs now using
            json extension.
            Waveshare relay board fully operational.
v26.02.07 - Protect OLED from multi-thread access.
            Initial Waveshare Relay board support (ESP32S3 with RS485).
            Fix flash programmer (python) flash size detection.
v26.02.06 - New Indicators - used in LCD and also in OLED screensaver.
            Fast detect no SSID configured for entry into AP mode.
            LCD not using PSRAM due to system impact, using SRAM bounce buffers
            only to maintain functionality (SPI bus contention occurs).
v26.02.05 - Flash programmer - force image bank for app only update.
          - UserIO updates only via control.
          - Preparation for LVGL integration
v26.02.04 - More build environment changes, no functional updates
v26.02.03 - Fix bug in Shelly EM3G sampling
v26.02.02 - Now using docker & arduino-cli build pipeline
v26.02.01 - Support the EM Gen3 Shelly device
v26.01.08 - Ensure thread safe fetching of event logs for the live view
            from the manager client.
v26.01.07 - Replace the invalidTarget processing with a new flag in the
            LG config, 'logHeatingTargetChanges', that will determine if
            target temperature changes are recored in the event log.  By
            default series 3 will not log such events.
v26.01.06 - Reduce max LG daily log events due to 75% SPIFFS usage.
          - Only display integer byte/KiB values in webserver file list.
v26.01.05 - Following testing on series 3 new invalid target temperature
            filtering provided (using invalidTarget and logInvalidEvents
            items for the LG heatpump JSON).
          - Fix background tint in live event view on error reports.
          - Error 0x8000 is an invalid LG data detected.
          - Fix lack on header on very first LG event log.
v26.01.04 - Try to avoid glitches in DHW and target temperature data for
            series 3.  There has to be 2 successive samples with the
            same sample value for the register to be read successfully.
          - Pull any RS485 enable low as early as possible during boot.
v26.01.03 - Fix live LG event view - force data reload via dummy parameter.
          - Support LG modbus event replay for testing.
            Requires additional library for modbus slave, modbus-esp8266.
v26.01.02 - Fix the Date field when sending email
v26.01.01 - Fix LG event log timestamps
v25.12.14 - LG event log processing improvements, 600 events per log,
            add new CSS for error conditions.
            Defensive closure of File's used by ReadyMail sending.
v25.12.13 - Rotate LG logs on daily update irrespective of email state.
          - Remove labels from each row of the current event view.
v25.12.12 - Fix incorrect FS type for LG daily email.
          - Avoid first sample returning garbage data.
v25.12.11 - Switch to ReadyMail library, fix html LG event entries.
            With this library we can send the HTML LG event log as email
            body, and clients such as gmail & outlook may then display
            the event log as opposed to opening the attachment.
v25.12.10 - LG Event log, restructure to reduce row size in file.
v25.12.09 - LG Event log - DHW priority, set to similar LG colour scheme
v25.12.08 - HTML format for LG event log, sent in email and new page
            available from the webserver.
          - New SSE events for future realtime view of updates.
          - Further CSS changes for look and feel/consistency.
          - LG event log limited to 480 events/day (protect flash).
v25.12.07 - New look and feel and improved client HTML/Javascript for a
            more coherrent experience and a more modern look.
            Fix SD daily update (file not starting at the update time).
            Fix the default h/w selection if no .hid file present.
            Early S3 RGB Led support.
v25.12.06 - Webserver reboot directly when in AP mode.
            Support esp32s3 gadget, UserIO to console.
v25.12.05 - Send stored data at daily update time.
            Rework the boards.txt to separate out custom boards from
            original Espressif esp32 release.
v25.12.04 - Fix webserver reboot from No WiFi on boot failure.
            Add Shelly data to stored samples.
            Show free memory not largest free block in debug logs.
v25.12.03 - Add timeouts to Shelly and OpenWeather HTTP requests.
v25.12.02 - Support Shelly EM and PMG3 energy monitors via their local
            HTTP servers.
            Support OpenWeather HTTP API to fetch local outdoor temp.
            Don't attempt a Dallas 1-wire acquisition if no DS18B20's
            found on the bus.
            Embed SSL certificates for emoncms and OpenWeather as opposed
            to using files in SPIFFS.
v25.11.01 - Fix reset processing
v25.09.08 - UDP remote. Add new AsyncUDP instance in networking for listening
            for temp. broadcast messages.  When sampling temps don't set
            invalid temperatures for remote sensors (would need timer to
            set invalid ideally).
            UPS3 heat meter - power of zero is valid.
            UDP loggging, limit msg to CONFIG_TCP_MSS size (1436 bytes)
            Reboot page restyle
v25.09.07 - UDP remote: Async_udp library needs patching to prevent call to
            ::listen() failing if the UDP task already exists
v25.09.06 - Reboot : New html for reboot, which occurs in loop thread after
            flag set from webserver.
            LG - any modbus error invalidates all register values in a sample.
            Measurement Sample.  Now has vectors for the 4 sensor types.
            Mutex protected last sample.  Sampling of sensors is independent
            of reading them.
            Debug/Message level changes to improve consistency.
            UserIO uses its own Sample instance to populate the display.
            No calls are made to sensor types to obtain additional data.
            UPS3 heat meter detects pump off condition.  If poor quality
            flow rate detected then not sent to emon (if number of PWM
            samples is < 70% of possible number, likely affected by context
            switching).
            Temperatures - remote data protected by new mutex.
v25.09.05 - Memory improvements:
               Stack size reductions (async_tcp, userIO, arduino_events)
               Map sensor type + ID to name
            Don't show LG data on OLED if sample has modbus error
v25.09.04 - Ensure manager webpage is in sync with current settings
v25.09.03 - Fix file upload, now returns to manager screen
            Fix statistics send in daily email (% calc. error)
            Only measure one sensor per sample period, record sample stats
            Oled display processing moved to separate thread
            Replaced temperature sensor mutex with sample mutex
            Debug section added to webserver for development diagnostics
            Reduced memory footprint of config to reclaim ~2kB
v25.09.02 - Display screen saver (due to some OLED's appearing to fade)
            Fix File upload return to home page, new checkbox for display screen saver
            Heat Meter and Power Meter measurements at 15s intervals
            Internal structural changes, improved separation of concerns
v25.09.01 - Rebuild due to upgrade/downgrade Arduino CLI and esp32.
            Now back to Arduino 2.3.4 and esp32 3.1.0
v25.08.05 - Set master modbus to slave mode during boot
v25.08.04 - Change temp from 60 to 75 deg for detecting DS18B20 error
v25.08.03 - fix brace matching in json file, initial support for Waveshare LCD,file hierarchy changes
v25.08.02 - Fix modbus stats percentage calculation in daily email update
v25.08.01 - Defensive changes to prevent invalid bad data sent to emon (modbus read error, bad DS18B20 data)
v25.02.01 - LG 1000 event log limit resets on daily basis. 24 day reboot reason added
v25.01.21 - email communication statistics no longer cummulative
v25.01.20 - Single email with lg data
v25.01.19 - not released
v25.01.18 - parse emonCMS response to feed insert to obtain error state
v25.01.17 - moved reset html to end of page with confirm text added
v25.01.16 - fix SD card detection using board type not from config.dat
v25.01.15 - fix temperatures recorded when device is lost off the 1-Wire bus
v25.01.14 - Reset handling improvements, board select via file, debug webpage
v25.01.13 - fast boot detection (prevent flash wear on continuous cycling)
v25.01.11 - rework temperatures, reset handling, improved serial debug at boot
v25.01.10 - new reboot code BOOT_SETUP for error in setup, OLED display reboot cause
